---
/**
 * The support page.
 *
 * It exists because the app links to it: `SupportApp` in swift-support-kit renders
 * Help items for the tracker, the feedback form and `siteURL + supportPath`, and
 * that last one lands here.
 *
 * Armada's page, in the other order. `preferIssueTracker` is true in
 * apps/apple/Drakar/Services/Support.swift: Drakar is a developer tool, and the
 * public tracker is where its users already are, so the tracker leads and the
 * private form, for reports that have to quote your own code, comes second.
 */
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import {
  APP_NAME,
  FEEDBACK_URL,
  GITHUB_NEW_ISSUE_URL,
  ISSUES_URL,
  PRICING,
  SITE_URL,
  SUPPORT_EMAIL,
  SUPPORT_EMAIL_HREF,
} from "../config";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "ContactPage",
  name: "Support",
  url: `${SITE_URL}/support/`,
  isPartOf: { "@id": `${SITE_URL}/#website` },
  publisher: { "@id": `${SITE_URL}/#organization` },
};

const h2 = "m-0 font-display text-[22px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em]";
const lead = "mt-5 mb-0 max-w-[62ch] text-[15px] leading-[1.65] text-fg-dim text-pretty";
const prose = "mt-4 mb-0 max-w-[62ch] text-[15px] leading-[1.65] text-fg-dim text-pretty";
const link = "underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-accent-hi";
const strong = "font-medium text-fg";
---

<Layout
  title={`Support · ${APP_NAME}`}
  description={`Get help with ${APP_NAME}: the public tracker, a private feedback form for reports that quote your own code, or email for licences.`}
  schema={schema}
>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="wrap max-w-[820px] py-20">
    <div class="mono text-accent">Support</div>
    <h1 class="mt-3 mb-0 font-display text-[clamp(28px,4.4vw,40px)] font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em]">
      Support
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 mb-0 max-w-[62ch] text-[16px] leading-[1.6] text-fg-dim text-pretty">
      Three ways in, and which one to use comes down to a single question:{" "}
      <strong class={strong}>does telling us what went wrong mean quoting your own work?</strong>
    </p>

    <section class="mt-14">
      <h2 class={h2}>A bug or an idea you are happy to share</h2>
      <p class={lead}>
        The <a href={ISSUES_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class={link}>public tracker</a> is shared
        by every Magenta Creations app, and has a folder for {APP_NAME}. It suits most things: a card that
        renders wrong, a Claude Code or Codex release that broke something, a feature request. It is
        public, so the answer is there for whoever asks next.{" "}
        <a href={GITHUB_NEW_ISSUE_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class={link}>Open an issue</a>.
      </p>
      <p class={prose}>
        Say which version of {APP_NAME}, which macOS, and which <code class="font-mono text-fg">claude</code>
        or <code class="font-mono text-fg">codex</code> version the session ran. The protocol {APP_NAME}
        speaks is undocumented and moves with each CLI release, so that last number is usually the
        answer.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14">
      <h2 class={h2}>Anything that quotes your own work</h2>
      <p class={lead}>
        A useful report sometimes has to include a file path, a prompt or a piece of a transcript. The <a
          href={FEEDBACK_URL}
          class={link}>feedback form</a
        > is private: no account is needed, and the email address is optional. Leave it blank and the
        report is anonymous.
      </p>
      <p class={prose}>
        <strong class={strong}>Choosing Send Feedback in the app does not send anything.</strong> It
        hands your browser a URL and stops. Everything that URL carries (the app version, the macOS
        version, the Mac model and the language) is visible in the address bar, and on the page as four
        fields you can edit or clear before pressing Send.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14">
      <h2 class={h2}>Licences and payment</h2>
      <p class={lead}>
        Email <a href={SUPPORT_EMAIL_HREF} class={link}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a> for a key that will not
        activate, a key you have lost, or a refund within the {PRICING.refundDays}-day window, no reason
        needed. A key is checked on your Mac and never sent anywhere, so a reply is the only way we can
        look at one: quote the address you bought with rather than the key itself.
      </p>
      <p class={prose}>
        What a key covers, and what the trial does, is set out in the{" "}
        <a href="/terms/" class={link}>licence terms</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14">
      <h2 class={h2}>What to expect</h2>
      <p class={lead}>
        Everything gets read, and most things get an answer within a few working days. {APP_NAME} is not
        made by Anthropic or OpenAI, so a problem with Claude Code or Codex themselves, your plan or your
        sign-in belongs with them.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
